@startuml seq-access-token
title Self-service access: email allowlist → personal bearer token

actor "Anyone on the internet" as who
participant "serve\nPOST /v1/access (NOT behind auth)" as serve
participant "ConfigMap allowed-emails\n(hot-reloaded)" as cm
participant "k8s Secret\nagentplane-serve-tokens" as sec

who -> serve : {"email":"you@corp.com"}\n<color:#CC0000><b>cleartext HTTP (F2)</b></color>
serve -> cm : allowed(email)?
alt not allowlisted
  serve --> who : 403 (denial logged — the only signal)
else allowlisted
  serve -> sec : loadTokens()
  alt token exists for this email
    serve --> who : <b>the SAME token as before</b> (idempotent)
    note right : an attacker who knows an allowlisted\naddress gets the legitimate user's live token (F7)
  else first time
    serve -> serve : newToken() = "apl_" + 24B crypto/rand  ✅
    serve -> sec : saveTokens()
    serve --> who : new token
  end
end

note over who, sec #FFE4E4
  <b>F7</b>: rate-limited now (10/min per IP, 5/min per email) — but still
  no second factor, so email alone remains the credential.
  <b>F1</b>: the resulting token can read/write <b>every user's</b> sessions,
  because no route compares the session to its owner.
  Verification is constant-time ✅ (subtle.ConstantTimeCompare).
end note
@enduml
